  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-11-07T09:21:12.522Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "On PICO Standalone, the in-game keyboard defaults to the Minimised View when it first appears in a session. As the text entry box isn't interactive on standalone VRChat, clicking on it does nothing where I would expect for it to open the system keyboard, or change the cursor location and highlight text as it does on the PC versions (functionality which all Standalone versions seem to lack, perhaps worth a feature request if not intentional?)\n\nCurrently, PICO users need to manually expand the keyboard each session. Curious as to why this change was made, as the 1518 Chatbox 2.0 changelogs say that \"mobile, desktop, and Pico\" will default to the Minimised View despite PICO being a VR platform. May be worth checking if Quest defaults to Minimised as well.",
